## Foundational Argument (Across the Portfolio)

The acceptance of modern sport by Muslim and postcolonial societies is not simply 
"assimilation" of Western values. It is a complex negotiation between:

- Global norms and local authenticity
- Secular universalism and Islamic jurisprudence  
- Colonial legacies and postcolonial agency
- Western feminist discourse and Muslim women's self-determination

This portfolio traces how these tensions play out across different national contexts, 
historical moments, and sporting arenas — from the Pan-Arab Games to the FIFA 
World Cup 2022, from Beijing 2008 to London 2012.

